   308	
   309	## Reusable knowledge
   310	
   311	- `uv` had to be installed via Homebrew before `uv sync` and `uv run` worked; local MLX behaved better with `chat_template_kwargs.enable_thinking=False`, and a preserved `messages` list is required for multi-turn CLI memory [Task 1]
   312	- For the chat API, SSE should use safe framing such as JSON or other line-safe payloads, and long-lived streams should not hold request-scoped DB sessions open after DB access is no longer needed [Task 2]
   313	- Local dev Postgres should be bound to `127.0.0.1:5432` for safety, and typed validation is preferred over raw dict handling in request schemas [Task 2]
   314	- Ant Design X is the preferred primitive set here for AI chat UI (`Bubble.List`, `Sender`, `ThoughtChain`), and the chat/debug layout works best as equal-height panes with independent scroll [Task 3]
   315	- The practical design-research path for this repo is official Ant Design token/Figma resources plus rendered screenshots, not feeding the whole antd repo into Claude Design [Task 3]
   316	- For node overrides, the strongest confidence comes from proving effect in both API-level verifiers and browser e2e: UI override applied, trace changes, tool-call count actually drops [Task 4]
   317	- The ToolTree can start collapsed, so browser tests must expand the correct branch before interaction or they will click the wrong target and misread the result [Task 4]
   318	- On detail pages, redundant legends are usually worse than explicit rows because the repo prefers one-source-of-truth terminology and direct placement of A2A / visibility / source information [Task 5]
   319	
   320	## Failures and how to do differently
   321	
   322	- Symptom: minimal CLI feels broken across turns. Cause: stateless loop dropped prior messages. Fix: preserve and resend the full `messages` history [Task 1]
   323	- Symptom: local MLX floods the stream with long reasoning output. Cause: Qwen thinking remained enabled. Fix: set `chat_template_kwargs.enable_thinking=False` for the minimal slice [Task 1]
   324	- Symptom: SSE/chat logic is fragile or unsafe. Cause: raw token text was streamed directly and validation stayed loose. Fix: use safe framing and typed schema validation, and close DB sessions before streaming when possible [Task 2]
   325	- Symptom: debug UI drifts out of sync or overwhelms the page. Cause: too much always-visible debug detail. Fix: use explicit panes and on-demand debug disclosure rather than a constant dump [Task 3]
   326	- Symptom: override tests pass without proving real behavior. Cause: they only inspected request payloads. Fix: verify the response trace and other user-visible effects, not just outbound shape [Task 4]
   327	- Symptom: helper copy confuses the user. Cause: a caption or legend paraphrases structure without adding meaning. Fix: remove it or replace it with concrete rows/values [Task 5]
